kpmcore (26.08.1-0ubuntu1oaxaca1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * Ubuntu's 26.08.1-0ubuntu1 rebuilt for @DISTRO_NAME@ with one patch,
    luks2-no-forced-sector-size.patch: drop the "--sector-size 4096" that
    KPMcore 26.08 adds to "cryptsetup luksFormat" (upstream commit 25d3a793,
    2026-02-09), so cryptsetup picks the encryption sector size itself: 4096
    on a drive with 4K physical sectors when the partition's size allows it,
    512 otherwise. With the forced value cryptsetup refuses a partition whose
    size is not a multiple of 4096 bytes ("Device size is not aligned to
    requested sector size"), and Calamares 3.3.14 aligns the partition only
    for "Erase disk" (Ubuntu's align-end-sector-to-4k.patch, LP: #2165428),
    not for "Replace a partition" or "Install alongside" (Calamares issues
    2480 and 2526). Seen on 2026-10-11 installing @DISTRO_NAME@ with
    encryption on the Legion laptop's fifth partition (docs/7, choice 11).
    debian/ is otherwise Ubuntu's, Maintainer included.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0500
